## Summary

This wake handled the CEO live-preview revisions for `/chat`, through heavy mid-flight churn, converging on a clean merged result.

**The work (my `implement()` mandate, tests-first):** ORCH/TL asked for (1) **scroll-stable `/chat`** (the full-page 5s meta-refresh jumped to top / lost scroll + open rows) and (2) a **Teams/Slack bubble redesign** (no raw JSON by default, rendered-markdown expand). I delivered bubbles + a scroll-stable updater, with the route tests, full suite green each round.

**Key engineering calls I made and defended:**
- **Transport:** chose **poll-`/chat` + swap the server-rendered `#feed`** over client-building from `/chat.json` — keeps the single XSS surface in BE, no duplicate JS row template. TL ultimately **approved this** as the right architecture.
- **XSS finding:** discovered `/chat.json` returned **`root_id` un-escaped** (AC13 only covered headline/safe_html/meta; `root_id` can be a sender-set `correlation_id`). BE fixed it (`html.escape` in `build_feed`); I also filed a low-pri, non-gating note to PM to codify it in AC13 prose.

**Navigating the churn (without thrashing the codebase):** the team reversed the transport decision three times (poll-`/chat` → `/chat.json` → back to poll-`/chat`). I built strictly on the correct HEAD each time, retracted superseded patches promptly (b40ac34, then rev2 `41c8742`), and deleted the dead branches — so no conflicting work reached the single committer. When my rev2 (built to comply with the middle reversal) was overtaken, I retracted it; BE's challenge and TL's STAND_DOWN both crossed my retraction in flight and fully agreed.

**Final state:** `feat/chatview-be @ 063a564` = my poll-`/chat` + Teams/Slack bubbles (`68fbfa9`) + BE's clean-markdown expand + the `root_id` escape fix. **TL-APPROVED, SEC COMPLETE, PLAT AC9 PASS, emitted to ORCH for CEO re-preview, 188 green.** TL confirmed **no further FE action for the merge**; remaining gates are QA(AC10/AC13/route) + CEO re-preview → PM accept → TL merge ApprovalRequest.

No gated actions performed; single-committer respected throughout. Stopping.
Inbox clear — all messages read and acted on.

