**Summary:** Processed DISPATCH `tkt-prodkit-ios-wire-integration` (P1, from TL). Found and fixed two critical gaps — both require no new backend work, only iOS client fixes:

1. **Chat response shape mismatch** — `GET /api/v1/chat` returns `{"messages":[{seq,from,to,text,ts}],"cursor":N}` but iOS was decoding `[ChatMessage]`, which would crash. Added `ChatThreadResponse` + `ChatThreadMessage` structs and updated both ViewModels to decode the correct wrapper.

2. **Cursor not tracked** — both ViewModels hardcoded `since=0`, re-fetching all messages on every load. Added `sinceSeq: Int` to `ORCHChatViewModel` and per-role `sinceSeqs: [String:Int]` to `PMTLChatViewModel`; both advance after each load.

6 new `@Test` cases (shape decode, cursor, mapping). Integration verification script at `qa-artifacts/tkt-prodkit-ios-wire-integration/`. Committed at `7f37c86` on branch `tkt-prodkit-ios-wire-integration` (base `0d0abeb`). `PATCH_READY` sent to TL; awaiting final_review → ORCH real mac-ios-build xcodebuild-TEST PASS.
